<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Apple requires a PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy file for App Store submissions.
	This app collects no data and does no tracking — everything (events,
	notes, photos) is stored locally on-device via SQLite/the filesystem,
	with the one exception of the user-initiated "Save to Photos" action,
	which writes to the user's own device library and isn't "collection"
	by Apple's definition (nothing leaves the device to any third party).

	IMPORTANT — verify before submitting:
	Xcode flags "required reason API" usage at Archive/upload time if any
	linked API needs a declared reason under NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes
	(e.g. certain FileManager timestamp/disk-space APIs, UserDefaults).
	As of this writing this app doesn't call any of those specific APIs
	(we use FileManager for basic read/write/delete, not timestamp or
	disk-space queries), so NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes is empty below.
	Re-check this the API list against Apple's current requirements before
	every submission, since Apple updates the required-reason API list
	periodically — search "Xcode privacy manifest required reason API"
	for the current list if unsure.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
